  "question": {
    "text": "<p>The difference between threshold wavelengths for two metal surfaces <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> having work function&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#981;</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn><mi>eV</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#981;</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>eV</mi></math> in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>nm</mi></math>&nbsp;is:</p><p>{Given, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>h</mi><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1242</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>eV</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>nm</mi></math>}</p>",
